  "plans": [
    {
      "hypothesis": "The boundary reading is what merges touching lamellae into wide blocks on this image, which looks like back-scattered-electron (BSE) TiAl. If so, the regions reading with flake-width scaling near the fine scale (about 10 px, from the regions profile) will make the real drawing's lamellae individual strips with median aspect ratio >= 5 (currently 2.96), and a regions twin can reach worst-family <= 1. If the median aspect ratio stays below about 5, merging is not a reading problem and the set should be marked unsupported.",
      "rationale": "The only real-image evidence is one review at about 0.7 confidence. It found no thin boundary lines, only touching strips of 3-4 grey levels, and it saw colour blocks spanning several lamellae. The twin shows the same pattern: aspect-ratio bias -0.30. The identical set (tial_lamellar_L26) already failed under the boundary reading, with twin holdout worst-family 2.78. The current twin is untrusted, and its 0.599 trials come from a phase-like configuration that does not resemble the image, so they say nothing about the real set.\n\nI therefore switch to regions, which rebuilds a BSE-like twin. Start-parameter choices:\n- flake_width_px goes back to auto so pixel parameters scale to the regions width.\n- min_area_px drops to the default, because 102 px may cut thin lamellae.\n- min_aspect_for_orientation rises to 2.0, partway toward the reviewer's suggested 3, to keep the equiaxed and grain-boundary-alpha blocks out of the statistics.\n\nSearch space:\n- h_px and merge_saddle_ratio control whether pieces are split or merged back.\n- merge_max_offaxis_deg sets the end-to-end test, which should stop side-by-side lamellae from merging.\n- sigma and flatten_px control whether faint grey-level steps survive.\n\nThe reviewer's suggested 'number of grey levels' parameter does not exist and is not used.\n\nScratch handling is a separate issue. Twin scratch recall is about 0, and no real scratch is visible on this image, so this search cannot validate it; it must be re-checked once the regions twin exists.\n\nConfidence that the switch fixes the merging: about 0.55. Confidence that this image is BSE TiAl rather than etched optical Ti-6Al-4V: about 0.7, taken from the reviewer, and I cannot verify it myself.",
      "reading": "regions",
      "flake_phase": "auto",
      "start_params_json": "{\"mode\": \"regions\", \"flake_width_px\": \"auto\", \"min_area_px\": 30, \"min_aspect_for_orientation\": 2.0, \"h_px\": 0.5, \"merge_saddle_ratio\": 0.5, \"sigma\": 1.0, \"flatten_px\": 40}",
      "search_space_json": "{\"h_px\": [0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0], \"merge_saddle_ratio\": [0.5, 0.7, 0.9, 1.0], \"merge_max_offaxis_deg\": [10, 20, 30], \"sigma\": [0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0], \"flatten_px\": [0, 40, 80], \"min_aspect_for_orientation\": [1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0]}"
