      "rationale": "The twin is untrusted: its coherence ratio is 1.31, its minority fraction ratio 1.40, and its method width ratio 1.55. No search runs, so only a small change backed by the reviewer's evidence is justified. I leave all other params at current best.\n\nWhat each change addresses:\n- The reviewer judged the regions reading correct. Keep it.\n- The reviewer saw large equiaxed patches coloured and counted. That points at min_aspect_for_orientation. I raise it only to 2.0, not the suggested 3, because 3 would also drop short lamella fragments and thin out the colonies.\n- The reviewer suspected fine lamellae merged across their width, with low confidence ('unsure at this resolution'). Smoothing is the param most directly tied to losing narrow grey-level steps, so sigma drops modestly to 0.8. The noise-to-contrast ratio is low (0.0145), so less smoothing should not add much spurious splitting.\n\nWhat I deliberately leave alone:\n- I do not touch merge or scratch params. The real image shows no scratches, so the reviewer cannot judge any scratch change.\n- The end-to-end merging the reviewer saw was on the twin, which does not resemble the real set.\n\nWhat the evidence does not support:\n- The real median width (7.99 px) is already below the profile width (10.2 px). That argues against global under-splitting, so the merging claim is weak.\n- None of these changes can resolve the scratch-score contradiction or the twin failures. The twin's worst family is 2.56 and scratch handling there is broken. Those need a twin rebuild, not a param change.\n\nThe search space below is given for the record, to be used if a trusted twin is ever built.",
